\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Lorenz-63 smoothing ($T=2000, D=3, N=512$). The learned full-covariance neural twist matches the EKF smoother (the analytic reference) and beats FFBSi by a wide margin in RMSE, while the parallel implementation cuts wall-clock by $2.8\times $ over the sequential twisted version.}}{10}{table.4}}
\newlabel{tab:lorenz63}{{4}{10}{Lorenz-63 smoothing ($T=2000, D=3, N=512$). The learned full-covariance neural twist matches the EKF smoother (the analytic reference) and beats FFBSi by a wide margin in RMSE, while the parallel implementation cuts wall-clock by $2.8\times $ over the sequential twisted version}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Lorenz-96 RMSE versus wall-clock at $D \in \{10, 20, 40\}$ ($T=2000, N=64$). The twisted smoother (sequential triangle, parallel star) maintains an essentially constant RMSE of $\approx 0.30$ as $D$ grows, while bootstrap PF and FFBSi degrade by an order of magnitude. The parallel point sits to the right of the sequential point at $D=20, 40$: a $0.3\times $/$0.1\times $ wall-clock slowdown that nevertheless dominates both baselines on the Pareto frontier.}}{10}{figure.5}}
\newlabel{fig:lorenz96}{{5}{10}{Lorenz-96 RMSE versus wall-clock at $D \in \{10, 20, 40\}$ ($T=2000, N=64$). The twisted smoother (sequential triangle, parallel star) maintains an essentially constant RMSE of $\approx 0.30$ as $D$ grows, while bootstrap PF and FFBSi degrade by an order of magnitude. The parallel point sits to the right of the sequential point at $D=20, 40$: a $0.3\times $/$0.1\times $ wall-clock slowdown that nevertheless dominates both baselines on the Pareto frontier}{figure.5}{}}
